I have a comprehensive picture. Here are my findings.

## Summary

The telephone/E.164 logic lives in the **OfficeFloor "owner" function package** plus the **Owner JPA model** and the **OpenAPI-generated `OwnerFieldsDto`**. There are two enforcement paths (a custom E.164 normalizer used on POST, and a Bean-Validation `@Pattern` on the entity), plus a duplicate-telephone check. Naming convention: owner request-pipeline steps are classes named `<Verb>Owner...` under `rest/function/owner/`, and rejections throw `*Exception` types under `rest/escalation/` handled by matching `*ExceptionHandler` classes wired via `officefloor/escalation/<FQCN>.yml`.

---

## 1. The E.164 validator/converter

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/E164Telephone.java`** — the core E.164 logic (package-private util). Full body:

```java
static String toE164(String raw) {
    if (raw == null) {
        return null;
    }
    boolean international = raw.trim().startsWith("+");
    String digits = raw.replaceAll("\\D", "");
    if (!international) {
        if (digits.startsWith("0")) {
            digits = digits.substring(1);
        }
        digits = "61" + digits;
    }
    if (digits.length() < 8 || digits.length() > 15) {
        return null;
    }
    return "+" + digits;
}
```

Key behavior: if input starts with `+`, it keeps all digits as-is (country code preserved). Otherwise it assumes Australia `+61`, dropping a single leading `0`. Returns `null` unless total digits after `+` is 8–15. **Note: it does NOT validate per-country national-number length** — it only checks the global 8–15 total-digit bound. So `+61 123` (`61`+`123` = 5 digits) returns null, but that check is length-of-total, not "+61 needs exactly 9 national digits."

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`** — invokes it and produces a 400 on failure:

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    String e164 = E164Telephone.toE164(owner.getTelephone());
    if (e164 == null) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(List.of("telephone"));
    }
    owner.setTelephone(e164);
}
```

---

## 2. DTO / request classes with a telephone field

- **`OwnerFieldsDto`** is NOT a source file — it is generated by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` (pom.xml line ~369) from `openapi.yml` into `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`. Its schema is in **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**, `OwnerFields` (lines 1991–2056):
  ```yaml
  telephone:
    title: Telephone number
    type: string
    minLength: 1
    maxLength: 20
    pattern: '^[0-9]*$'      # digits only — no '+' allowed at DTO layer
    example: '6085551023'
  ...
  required:
    - firstName
    - lastName
    - address
    - city
